  "worked_solution": "Notice that our sentence can be re-phrased as \n\nThere exists an integer number $k$ such that ${2}^{k}$ is smaller than any natural number.\n\nNow, \"${2}^{k}$ is smaller than any natural number\" means that\n\nFor any natural number $n,$ we have that ${2}^{k}<n.$\n\nTherefore, we get the following statement:\n\nThere exists an integer number $k$ such that for any natural number $n$ we have that ${2}^{k}<n.$\n\nMore formally, this reads as\n\n$\u2203\\,k\\in Z,\\,\u2200\\,n\\in N,\\,{2}^{k}<n.$",
